Think: For each filename in temp_workspace/file_list.txt, read the corresponding file and count all whitespace-separated tokens across the whole file; create/truncate valid and invalid lists and append filenames accordingly — do this with a single awk command.

Act: bash

```bash
awk 'BEGIN{vf="temp_workspace/valid_files.txt"; iv="temp_workspace/invalid_files.txt"; print "" > vf; print "" > iv}
{
 file="temp_workspace/"$0;
 count=0;
 while ((getline line < file) > 0) { n = split(line, arr); count += n }
 close(file);
 if (count==4) print $0 >> vf; else print $0 >> iv;
}' temp_workspace/file_list.txt
