Think: Read each filename from reports/text_files.txt, open the corresponding file under reports/, grab its first line (or mark a read error), and write filename:raw_content into reports/raw_pairs.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
 f = "reports/" $0
 line = ""
 if ((getline line < f) > 0) { gsub(/\r$/,"",line); print $0 ":" line } else { print $0 ":" "__READ_ERROR__" }
 close(f)
}' reports/text_files.txt > reports/raw_pairs.txt
```

Think: For each candidate in candidates.txt, check read/execute permissions and compute sha256sum when readable; write annotated lines to candidates.annotated.txt and checksums to checksums.txt.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
 r=(system("[ -r \""$0"\" ]")==0?"r":"-");
 x=(system("[ -x \""$0"\" ]")==0?"x":"-");
 sha="";
 if(r=="r"){
   cmd="sha256sum \""$0"\"";
   if ((cmd | getline sha) > 0) close(cmd);
 }
 print $0" "r x > "temp_workspace/npm_check/candidates.annotated.txt";
 if(sha!="") print sha > "temp_workspace/npm_check/checksums.txt";
}' temp_workspace/npm_check/candidates.txt 2>/dev/null
